port tool is preserved. I tested it in Blender 5.3.0 on our own Screen 05 model, and it aligned, measured and scaled it correctly. Splat files (`.ply`/`.spz`) can now be stored in the repo the same way as the other large 3D files, which avoids GitHub's 100 MB file limit. The tool reads `.glb` meshes and `.ply` splats, so if Marble gives you only `.spz`, export a `.glb` or `.ply` too. Ways to get the files to me are listed in `qa/worldlabs/05/MARBLE_MANUAL.md`:\n- attach them in the chat,\n- upload them to `qa/worldlabs/05/import/` on GitHub (25 MB per file through the website),\n- or send a download link; I'd then ask your approval to allow that one website.\n\n**Autosave:** pushed and verified at `eadf7d8`, with GitHub matching the local copy. This also needed one fix: the new environment was blocking the host GitHub uses to store large 3D files, so the re-exported Benny model wasn't backing up. I allowed that single host (`lfs.github.com`), and new models now back up normally.\n\nThe game wasn't restarted. The environment, water, foam and Benny specialists are still working on Screen 05 from their saved progress, using Blender and the Playwright captures. I'll send the comparisons, test results and final commit when they finish.", "type": "text"}], "context_management": null, "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011Ch5UDvfdfYedetATzcc5d", "input_transformations": [], "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1374, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1374, "cache_read_input_tokens": 254673, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1374, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1374, "cache_read_input_tokens": 254673, "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1094, "type": "message